{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1350,
 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Gordon Glitz gave his new jet forty square windows. With curtains.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.762
  },
  {
   "text": "If the test flight worked, his face went on every tail.",
   "s": 3.962,
   "e": 6.425
  },
  {
   "text": "Pia the intern held up a donut. Gordon ignored the donut.",
   "s": 6.625,
   "e": 9.669
  },
  {
   "text": "He had eleven design awards. One was for \"Best Hair.\"",
   "s": 9.869,
   "e": 12.438
  },
  {
   "text": "So the jet took off: pilot Doug, and three hundred rubber chickens in seat belts.",
   "s": 12.558,
   "e": 16.622
  },
  {
   "text": "But up high, a tiny crack appeared. In a corner.",
   "s": 16.822,
   "e": 18.907
  },
  {
   "text": "Then every corner cracked, like lightning drawn by a toddler.",
   "s": 19.107,
   "e": 21.7
  },
  {
   "text": "Gordon's fix: forty rolls of duct tape, in the shape of his signature.",
   "s": 21.9,
   "e": 25.15
  },
  {
   "text": "Until window seven popped out like toast, and twelve chickens left early.",
   "s": 25.55,
   "e": 29.29
  },
  {
   "text": "Why the corners? Up high, the air inside pushes on every window.",
   "s": 29.49,
   "e": 32.637
  },
  {
   "text": "A sharp corner traps that push in one point, like a crowd in a doorway.",
   "s": 32.837,
   "e": 36.263
  },
  {
   "text": "A round window has no corner. Cracks have nowhere to start.",
   "s": 36.463,
   "e": 39.443
  },
  {
   "text": "Now Pia's donut is on every tail. Gordon got a window seat.",
   "s": 39.643,
   "e": 43.264
  }
 ],
